{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"Reconciled the settled dispute fix in the spine registries only.\n\n- `LLR-364` — `detail` amended.\n  - Before: “...whose whole approved and routed traced cell sets at the range's after revision equal that row's approved-snapshot copy at that revision.”\n  - After: “...equal that row's approved-snapshot copy at that revision, and for which either no entry the range added after the latest re-attesting one records a copy of that row's registry or omits its copy record ... or the row's routed traced cells at the after revision equal those at the before revision.”\n  - Added the explanation that later copying cannot absorb an unattested approved-cell change, and that the two arms work for squashed or unsquashed ranges. This states the implemented settlement condition without naming implementation carriers.\n\n- `TC-403` — `method` amended.\n  - Before: the method ended its named cases with `test_an_unrouted_traced_cell_moved_after_the_act_still_settles, and test_the_two_real_redundant_landings_mint_nothing`.\n  - After: it additionally names the five later-writer tests, including squashed/unsquashed same-registry and other-registry contrasts, legacy-entry behavior, and moved/unmoved routed-cell cases.\n  - Why: the method now describes every implemented regression and both condition arms.\n\n- `TC-403` — `expected` amended.\n  - Before: “Satisfies SR-178 AcceptanceCriteria through the LLR-364 filtering contract and IF-091 call outcome.”\n  - After: “Satisfies SR-178 AcceptanceCriteria through the LLR-364 filtering contract, both arms of its later-writer condition included over squashed and unsquashed ranges, and IF-091 call outcome.”\n  - Why: makes the intended coverage observable.\n\n- `IF-091` — `data` amended.\n  - Before: “...over the act ledger (IF-220) and snapshot copies...”\n  - After: “...over the act ledger (IF-220, each added entry's re-attested rows and `copied` registries), snapshot copies and the registries at base and head...”\n  - Why: the interface contract now names all data inputs used by settlement.\n\nBuilder-list reconciliation:\n\n- Confirmed the updated `LLR-364.code_symbol` list against the settled implementation.\n- Confirmed all 19 `TC-403.evidence` functions exist in `tests/test_intake_settled.py`.\n- Confirmed and applied the proposed `LLR-364.detail`, `TC-403.method`, `TC-403.expected`, and `IF-091.data` wording.\n- Left `LLR-153` and `LLR-158` unchanged; the fix does not make either amended sentence untrue.\n- No further spine row required amendment.\n\nChecks run:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict` — exit 0; `check_trajectory: clean`.\n- `trace.py --strict` — exit 0; `orphans=0 integrity=0`.\n- Skipped pytest as directed.\n\nThis was not a decomposition round, so no hat outcomes apply."}}
